{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/810262-demon-translation-guide","id":810262,"title":"Demon translation guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-16T09:18:37-08:00","id":810262,"title":"Demon translation guide","content":"I know it's only 5 bucks, but I'm just wondering if this book is good/worth it? I love both Demon games, but am a little partial to Fallen. Anyway, yay or nay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T10:39:00-08:00","id":810284,"title":"","content":"Definitely Yay. Each game is great, but the various synths of the two are amazingly compelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T10:46:13-08:00","id":810286,"title":"","content":"I found it the most solid of the translation guides, although it has one or two significant omissions for running Fallen (namely, Storytelling System rules for being ejected from the host and vulnerable to devouring before you find a new host are absent, and there's not much in the way of specifics for the yields of thralls). But it's very good for additional widgets to be able to import from one game to the other, it's thorough (covering player's guide material from both Fallen and Descent, so custom apocalyptic forms are addressed and supported), and unlike the other translation guides, it has a chapter of several possible setups and explanations for how the two very different types of demon could encounter one another in the same setting, if you want to see what happens when the two collide.<br /> <br /> So for five bucks, if you're already interested in it, I'd say go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}